Major features of the ENDF/B-VII.1 evaluation are:                9440 1451   31
                                                                  9440 1451   32
1. New covariance evaluations of nubar and the total, (n,gamma),  9440 1451   33
and (n,f) cross sections that utilize ENDF/B-VII standards data   9440 1451   34
are incorporated. All available experimental data was included in 9440 1451   35
each covariance analysis, using the GLUCS code by Hetrick and Fu  9440 1451   36
(He80).  The output included most probable cross sections or      9440 1451   37
multiplicities, standard deviations, and correlations.            9440 1451   38
                                                                  9440 1451   39
2. A new ORNL evaluation (July 2010) was performed, extending the 9440 1451   40
resolved resonance range up to 5.7 keV.                           9440 1451   41
                                                                  9440 1451   42
3. A new prompt fission neutron spectrum evaluation was performed 9440 1451   43
using the Los Alamos model, as well as an uncertainty             9440 1451   44
quantification study for the 0.5 MeV neutron-induced spectrum.    9440 1451   45
                                                                  9440 1451   46
4. New reaction theory calculations are utilized for (n,xn) and   9440 1451   47
other reactions.  Direct reaction cross sections and angular      9440 1451   48
distributions are extended to an excitation energy of 4 MeV based 9440 1451   49
on the 238U ENDF/B-VII evaluation.                                9440 1451   50
                                                                  9440 1451   51
5. Fission product yields, delayed-neutron data, and photon-      9440 1451   52
production data are carried over from ENDF/B-VII.                 9440 1451   53
                                                                  9440 1451   54
6. Uncertainty quantification of all major reaction cross-sections9440 1451   55
(MF=33, MT=1,2,4,16,17,18,102) and of the prompt fission neutron  9440 1451   56
spectrum (MF=35, MT=18) and prompt fission neutron multiplicity   9440 1451   57
(MF=31, MT=456).                                                  9440 1451   58
