a1, J. Nuclear Energy, 22,299,968) which were the basis of the    9440 1451  115
identification of the resonances in the Bouland-Derrien           9440 1451  116
evaluation. Consequently much more resonances were identified     9440 1451  117
in the new evaluation mainly p-wave resonances. Due to a lack of  9440 1451  118
time, Weston fission data were not included in the data base: the 9440 1451  119
fission widths obtained in the Bouland-Derrien evaluation were    9440 1451  120
kept for most of them. All the experimental data available at     9440 1451  121
thermal energies were included in the new evaluation.             9440 1451  122
  The cross sections in the energy range from thermal to 5700 ev  9440 1451  123
neutron energy were well represented by 554 resonances: 549       9440 1451  124
resonances in the energy range 0 to 5700 eV, 5 fictitious negative9440 1451  125
